        <mxCell id="note" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Architecture notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Layers: Controller → Service → Repository (Spring Data JPA) → Entity. Controllers exchange only Request/Response DTOs. CRUD controllers follow XxxController → XxxService → XxxRepository (omitted).&lt;br&gt;• Persisted tables: users, members, residences, devices, device_members (join table of the Member–Device many-to-many) and consumption_history.&lt;br&gt;• Profile is abstract (@MappedSuperclass): User and Member inherit id, name, email, photoUrl, createdAt.&lt;br&gt;• Device always belongs to a User (owner) and optionally to a Residence. It can be shared by several Members; its cost is split equally among them.&lt;br&gt;• Consumption: kWh/month = (powerW × hoursPerDay × daysPerMonth) / 1000; cost = kWh × Residence.tariffKwh.&lt;br&gt;• Limit and alert are not classes: Residence holds monthlyKwhLimit, monthlyCostLimit and alertThresholdPercent; ConsumptionService.getLimitStatus() computes a LimitStatus DTO (usagePercent, level OK/WARNING/EXCEEDED) on demand.&lt;br&gt;• Report is a DTO built from ConsumptionHistory. DeviceOffer is fetched live from the marketplaces (no table) and a new store means a new adapter only.&lt;br&gt;• Fixed value sets (category, availability, level) are plain Strings in the model; use enums in code if you want, they do not need a box here." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="1200" x="40" y="2060" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
